# ============================================================
#  Generic social events — `actor: any`.
#  The engine binds `npc` to one met character for whom `when`
#  is true. Use rel(npc), love(npc), bond(npc), romanceable(npc),
#  tagged(npc, faculty) in conditions and {npc}, {they}, {them},
#  {their}, {They} in text. These drive the relationship system:
#  friendships form, romances spark, rivalries flare, bonds decay.
# ============================================================

# ---------------- Friendship ----------------

@event soc_study_session
title: Study Session
class: windfall
tone: light
cast:
  npc: any where not tagged(npc, faculty) and rel(npc) >= 0
per: npc
trigger: social
repeat: 4
art: book
tags: social study
scene: Two students at a candlelit table piled with books, one explaining something with wild hand gestures.
text: {npc} drops into the seat across from you with an armful of books. "Exams are coming for us all. Misery loves company. Study with me?"
> left: You work better alone
  lore +tiny
  rel npc -tiny
  say: You get a lot done. {npc} sits at the next table and sighs loudly every few minutes.
> right: Pull up a chair
  lore +small
  study +tiny
  rel npc +small
  say: You get half as much done and remember twice as much of it. {npc} explains the Third Law with a biscuit diagram.

@event soc_borrow_money
title: A Small Loan
class: routine
tone: light
cast:
  npc: any where not tagged(npc, faculty) and rel(npc) >= 3
per: npc
trigger: social
when: gold >= 20
repeat: 6
art: pouch
tags: social money
scene: A student holding out an empty purse upside down with a sheepish grin.
text: {npc} turns out an empty purse. "I'm fifteen crowns short for rent. I'll pay you back. I swear on my wand."
> left: Sorry, you're tight too
  rel npc -small
  say: "No, of course, I understand." {They} {are} quiet at dinner.
> right: Lend fifteen crowns
  gold -medium
  rel npc +medium
  chance 70:
    queue soc_loan_repaid in 2 with npc
    say: {npc} hugs you with the empty purse still in {their} hand.
  else:
    say: {npc} hugs you. You suspect you will never see those fifteen crowns again.

@event soc_loan_repaid
title: Paid Back
class: story
tone: light
trigger: queued
actor: npc
art: coin
tags: social money
scene: A small stack of coins and a sweet bun left on a desk with a thank-you note.
text: {npc} finds you after class and presses a little stack of coins into your hand, plus a sticky bun. "Fifteen crowns. And interest." The interest is the bun.
> ok: Eat the interest
  gold +medium
  rel npc +small
  mood +tiny

@event soc_become_friends
title: Something Like Friendship
class: milestone
tone: light
cast:
  npc: any where bond(npc) == "none" and rel(npc) >= 18 and not tagged(npc, faculty)
per: npc
trigger: social
weight: 20
art: group
tags: social
scene: Two students walking across the lawn at sunset, laughing at the same joke, shadows long behind them.
text: You realise you've been looking for {npc} in every room you walk into. {They} seem to have been doing the same. Somewhere along the way, this became a friendship.
> left: Keep a little distance
  rel npc +tiny
  say: You stay friendly. Just not too close. Some walls are load-bearing.
> right: Call it what it is
  bond npc friend
  rel npc +medium
  mood +small
  say: "So we're friends now," {npc} says. "Officially." You shake on it, solemnly, then ruin it by laughing.

@event soc_become_close
title: The Kind of Friend You Call at 3am
class: milestone
tone: light
cast:
  npc: any where bond(npc) == "friend" and rel(npc) >= 36
per: npc
trigger: social
weight: 18
art: heart
tags: social
scene: Two friends sitting on a dormitory floor at 3am wrapped in one blanket, empty mugs between them.
text: It's 3am. You can't sleep, and you've walked to {npc}'s door before you've even decided to. {They} open{s} it before you knock.
> left: Apologise and go back to bed
  rel npc +small
  say: "Don't be daft," {npc} says, but lets you go. In the morning there's tea outside your door.
> right: Talk until sunrise
  bond npc close
  rel npc +medium
  mood +medium
  say: You tell {them} things you haven't told anyone. {They} tell you things back. The sun comes up and neither of you notices.

@event soc_secret
title: A Secret
class: windfall
tone: light
cast:
  npc: any where rel(npc) >= 15 and not tagged(npc, faculty)
per: npc
trigger: social
repeat: 8
art: lock
tags: social
scene: Two students huddled under a staircase, one whispering into the other's ear, a finger to their lips.
text: {npc} pulls you under the stairs. "I need to tell someone or I'll burst. Swear you won't tell anyone. Not even the portraits."
> left: "I'd rather not carry it."
  rel npc -tiny
  say: {npc} looks hurt, then relieved. "Maybe that's better." You'll never know.
> right: "I swear."
  rel npc +medium
  guile +tiny
  say: It's not a big secret. It's the kind that's only big to the person holding it. You hold it with {them}.

@event soc_argument
title: Words Exchanged
class: routine
tone: light
cast:
  npc: any where rel(npc) >= 6 and bond(npc) != "partner"
per: npc
trigger: social
repeat: 6
weight: 8
art: bolt
tags: social
scene: Two students facing off in an empty corridor, one with arms crossed, the other mid-gesture, both flushed.
text: It starts with something small — a borrowed book, a joke that landed wrong — and suddenly you and {npc} are arguing in the corridor, louder than either of you intended.
> left: Apologise first
  rel npc +small
  mood -tiny
  say: "I'm sorry." {npc} deflates. "...Me too." It's over. It feels better than winning would have.
> right: Stand your ground
  rel npc -medium
  mood -tiny
  chance 50:
    say: {npc} storms off. You were right. It doesn't feel as good as you'd hoped.
  else:
    rel npc +medium
    say: You argue it out until you're both laughing at how ridiculous it got. Somehow you're closer after.

@event soc_village_trip
title: A Day in the Village
class: routine
tone: light
cast:
  npc: any where rel(npc) >= 6 and not tagged(npc, faculty)
per: npc
trigger: social
when: gold >= 5
repeat: 5
art: house
tags: social
scene: A cobbled village street with crooked shopfronts, two students sharing a paper cone of roasted nuts.
text: "Barge to the village? Tea at Mabel's, a wander round the bookshops, back before curfew?" {npc} is already wearing {their} coat.
> left: Not this week
  rel npc -tiny
  say: {They} bring{s} you back a cinnamon bun anyway.
> right: Grab your coat
  gold -tiny
  mood +medium
  rel npc +small
  say: Tea, buns, a bookshop cat that sits on {npc}'s feet. You almost miss the last barge, laughing.

@event soc_friend_sick
title: Sick Friend
class: windfall
tone: light
cast:
  npc: any where (bond(npc) == "friend" or bond(npc) == "close" or bond(npc) == "partner")
per: npc
trigger: social
repeat: 8
art: rain
tags: social
scene: A student tucked into an infirmary bed under a mountain of blankets, a friend sitting beside them with a bowl of soup.
text: {npc} has Lake Fever and is miserable in the infirmary. Sister Amaranth says visitors are allowed, but she won't be responsible.
> left: Send a card
  rel npc +tiny
  say: You send a card with a drawing of Sister Amaranth as a dragon. {npc} keeps it on {their} bedside table.
> right: Sit with them every evening
  rel npc +medium
  chance 35:
    gain sick
    say: You keep {them} company for a week. Then you're in the next bed. You both find this hilarious.
  else:
    say: You read aloud, badly, doing voices. {npc} recovers and claims it was the voices.

@event soc_gift_given
title: A Small Gift
class: routine
tone: light
cast:
  npc: any where rel(npc) >= 9
per: npc
trigger: social
repeat: 7
art: gem
tags: social
scene: A small wrapped parcel tied with ribbon left on a dormitory pillow, a pressed flower tucked into the bow.
text: There's a small parcel on your pillow. A note in {npc}'s handwriting: "Saw this and thought of you. Don't make it weird."
> left: Thank {them} later
  mood +small
  rel npc +tiny
  say: It's a tiny brass compass that always points to the nearest teapot. You use it constantly.
> right: Get {them} something back (10 gold)
  gold -small
  mood +small
  rel npc +medium
  say: You find {them} a book {they}'d wanted for months. {npc}'s face when {they} open{s} it is worth twice the price.

@event soc_drift
title: Drifting Apart
class: windfall
tone: light
cast:
  npc: any where rel(npc) >= 6 and rel(npc) < 24 and not tagged(npc, faculty)
per: npc
trigger: social
when: since(soc_drift) > 3
weight: 6
repeat: 6
art: hourglass
tags: social
scene: A student glancing back across a busy courtyard at another who hasn't seen them, the space between them full of strangers.
text: You realise you haven't really talked to {npc} in weeks. You see {them} across the courtyard, laughing with people you don't know.
> left: Let it be
  rel npc -small
  say: People drift. It's nobody's fault. You still smile when you pass in the halls.
> right: Go over and say hello
  rel npc +medium
  mood +tiny
  say: "There you are!" {npc} says, as if you'd been the one missing. Maybe you had.

@event soc_rumour
title: Rumours About {npc}
class: routine
tone: light
cast:
  npc: any where rel(npc) >= 9
per: npc
trigger: social
repeat: 8
art: paper
tags: social
scene: A cluster of students whispering behind their hands in a corridor, glancing toward someone just out of view.
text: A nasty rumour about {npc} is going round the common room. It's not true. You know it's not true. People are laughing.
> left: Let it blow over
  rel npc -tiny
  say: It blows over. {npc} never finds out you heard it. Probably.
> right: Shut it down
  challenge negotiate trivial:
    win:
      rel npc +medium
      renown +small
      say: You make the rumour-monger look so foolish that the story dies on the spot. {npc} hears about it later and just squeezes your arm.
    lose:
      rel npc +small
      renown -tiny
      say: You make a scene and now there are rumours about you too. {npc} thinks you're an idiot. A loyal idiot.

@event soc_homework_help
title: Desperate Homework
class: routine
tone: light
cast:
  npc: any where not tagged(npc, faculty) and rel(npc) >= 0
per: npc
trigger: social
repeat: 5
art: feather
tags: social study
scene: A student with ink on their face clutching a half-finished essay, another student leaning over to read it.
text: {npc} waves a half-finished essay at you. "It's due in an hour and I've written the title twice. Help."
> left: Explain the concept
  challenge research easy:
    win:
      rel npc +medium
      lore +tiny
      say: You explain it so clearly that {npc} finishes the essay with time to spare. {They} insist{s} you're a genius.
    lose:
      rel npc +tiny
      say: You explain it so confusingly that you both end up more lost. You hand it in together, two confused people against the world.
> right: "Copy mine."
  alignment -tiny
  rel npc +small
  chance 30:
    study -small
    rel npc -tiny
    say: The professor notices two identical essays. You both get detention, and a lecture.
    gain detention
  else:
    say: {npc} hands it in and gets a better mark than you did. Unbelievable.

@event soc_faculty_advice
title: A Word of Advice
class: windfall
tone: light
cast:
  npc: any where tagged(npc, faculty) and rel(npc) >= 6
per: npc
trigger: social
repeat: 6
art: scroll
tags: study
scene: A professor walking with a student along a covered walkway, pointing at something in an open book.
text: {npc} catches you after a lecture. "You've been working hard. Or hardly working. I can never tell with your year. Some advice, if you'll take it?"
> left: Politely decline
  rel npc -tiny
  say: "Suit yourself." {They} walk{s} off. Faculty have long memories.
> right: Listen carefully
  rel npc +small
  study +small
  lore +tiny
  say: It's good advice. Annoyingly good. Your next essay is better for it.

# ---------------- Romance ----------------

@event soc_spark
title: A Spark
class: windfall
tone: warm
cast:
  npc: any where romanceable(npc) and rel(npc) >= 9 and spark(npc) < 12 and bond(npc) != "partner"
per: npc
trigger: social
weight: 12
repeat: 6
art: sparkle
tags: social romance
scene: Two hands brushing as they reach for the same quill, both students freezing for a heartbeat.
text: You reach for the same quill as {npc}. Your hands touch. Neither of you lets go immediately. It's a perfectly ordinary quill.
> left: Laugh it off
  rel npc +tiny
  say: "All yours," you say. {npc} laughs. The moment passes. Mostly.
> right: Hold on a moment longer
  spark npc +medium
  rel npc +tiny
  say: {npc} looks up. Something in {their} face shifts. Then {they} let{s} go, a little pink, and the quill rolls under the desk.

@event soc_date
title: An Invitation
class: routine
tone: warm
cast:
  npc: any where romanceable(npc) and spark(npc) >= 12 and spark(npc) < 40 and bond(npc) != "partner" and rel(npc) >= 9
per: npc
trigger: social
weight: 12
repeat: 4
art: heart
tags: social romance
scene: A student nervously holding out a hand-drawn ticket to the village's floating lantern show.
text: You could ask {npc} to the lantern show in the village this weekend. As friends. Or, you know. Not as friends.
> left: Ask as friends
  rel npc +small
  mood +small
  say: It's a lovely evening. You're both very careful about elbows.
> right: Ask as more than friends
  if spark(npc) >= 25:
    challenge negotiate trivial:
      win:
        spark npc +medium
        mood +medium
        say: {npc} says yes before you finish the sentence. You hold hands through the whole show and miss every lantern.
      lose:
        spark npc -tiny
        mood -small
        say: {npc} hesitates, then says {they}'d rather go as friends. It's a nice evening. It's a long evening.
  else:
    challenge negotiate easy:
      win:
        spark npc +medium
        mood +medium
        say: {npc} says yes before you finish the sentence. You hold hands through the whole show and miss every lantern.
      lose:
        spark npc -tiny
        mood -small
        say: {npc} hesitates, then says {they}'d rather go as friends. It's a nice evening. It's a long evening.

@event soc_confess_generic
title: Feelings, Spoken
class: milestone
tone: warm
cast:
  npc: any where romanceable(npc) and spark(npc) >= 30 and rel(npc) >= 18 and bond(npc) != "partner" and bond(npc) != "ex"
per: npc
trigger: social
weight: 10
art: heart
tags: romance
scene: Two students standing very close on a windswept bridge between towers, one with a hand over their heart.
text: On the bridge between the towers, the wind snatching at your robes, you realise you can't keep it in anymore. {npc} is looking at you like {they} know what you're about to say.
> left: Say nothing
  spark npc -small
  say: The moment passes. You walk back together, a careful inch apart.
> right: Tell {them}
  challenge negotiate trivial:
    win:
      bond npc partner
      spark npc +medium
      mood +large
      say: "Finally," {npc} says, and kisses you, and the wind steals your breath anyway.
    lose:
      spark npc -large
      mood -medium
      say: {npc} takes a long breath. "I care about you," {they} say{s}. "Just not like that. I'm sorry." The wind is very cold.

@event soc_partner_date
title: Date Night
class: windfall
tone: warm
cast:
  npc: any where bond(npc) == "partner"
per: npc
trigger: social
repeat: 3
weight: 14
art: candle
tags: romance
scene: Two people at a tiny candlelit table in a window alcove of a village tea shop, snow falling outside.
text: {npc} has booked the window table at Mabel's. Candles. Snow outside. "I'm paying," {they} say{s}. "Don't argue."
> left: Talk about the future
  spark npc +small
  mood +medium
  say: You talk about where you'll be in ten years. In every version, you're both there.
> right: Talk about absolutely nothing
  spark npc +tiny
  mood +medium
  say: You argue for an hour about whether a hotdog is a sandwich. It is the best date of your life.

@event soc_partner_neglect
title: "You're Always Busy"
class: routine
tone: warm
cast:
  npc: any where bond(npc) == "partner"
per: npc
trigger: social
when: since(soc_partner_date) >= 5
weight: 14
repeat: 5
art: hourglass
tags: romance
scene: A person waiting alone at a table set for two, a candle burned low, the other chair empty.
text: {npc} is waiting outside your door. "I feel like I only see you in corridors," {they} say{s}. "Do you even want this?"
> left: "I'm sorry. I'll make time."
  spark npc +tiny
  mood -tiny
  study -tiny
  say: You skip a study session for a long walk by the lake. It's the right call.
> right: "You know how busy I am."
  spark npc -medium
  rel npc -medium
  say: {npc} nods slowly. Something between you cools a degree.

@event soc_breakup
title: The End of Something
class: routine
tone: grim
cast:
  npc: any where bond(npc) == "partner" and spark(npc) < 25
per: npc
trigger: social
weight: 30
art: heartbreak
tags: romance crisis
scene: Two people sitting on opposite ends of a bench in a grey garden, not looking at each other, rain beginning.
text: {npc} sits down at the far end of the bench. "I think we both know," {they} say{s} quietly. "This isn't working anymore."
> left: Fight for it
  challenge negotiate trivial:
    win:
      spark npc +large
      say: You talk for hours. It's raw and honest and it hurts. And at the end, {npc} takes your hand again.
    lose:
      bond npc ex
      gain heartbroken
      rel npc -large
      say: You try. It only makes it harder. In the end you're both crying, and it's over anyway.
> right: Let {them} go
  bond npc ex
  gain heartbroken
  rel npc +small
  say: You agree. It's terrible and gentle and right. {npc} kisses your forehead once before {they} leave{s}.

@event soc_two_timing
title: Found Out
class: routine
tone: grim
cast:
  npc: any where bond(npc) == "partner"
per: npc
trigger: social
when: bonds(partner) >= 2
weight: 40
art: heartbreak
tags: romance crisis
scene: A person holding up two crumpled love letters in a crowded corridor, the crowd parting around them.
text: {npc} is holding two letters. One is to {them}. The other isn't. "I found it in your bag," {they} say{s}, very quietly. Half the corridor has stopped to watch.
> left: Beg forgiveness
  challenge negotiate easy:
    win:
      spark npc -large
      rel npc -large
      say: {npc} doesn't forgive you. But {they} don't leave. Not yet. You're on borrowed time.
    lose:
      bond npc ex
      rel npc -huge
      renown -medium
      gain heartbroken
      say: {npc} tears both letters in half and walks away. Everyone knows by dinner.
> right: Say nothing
  bond npc ex
  rel npc -huge
  renown -medium
  say: Your silence is an answer. {npc} drops the letters at your feet and leaves. The story is all over the academy.

@event soc_ex_encounter
title: Awkward
class: milestone
tone: warm
cast:
  npc: any where bond(npc) == "ex"
per: npc
trigger: social
repeat: 6
art: mirror
tags: romance
scene: Two people coming face to face in a narrow library aisle, both holding books, neither moving.
text: You turn into the library aisle and there's {npc}. Your ex. Holding the same book you came for. Neither of you moves.
> left: Turn around and leave
  mood -tiny
  say: You find a different book in a different aisle and read the same paragraph six times.
> right: Say hello like a person
  rel npc +medium
  challenge negotiate trivial:
    win:
      bond npc friend
      say: It's awkward for one minute, then it isn't. You end up laughing about the time the dummy caught fire. Friends, maybe. Really.
    lose:
      mood -tiny
      say: "Hello." "Hello." You both stand there. Then you both leave. It's a start.

# ---------------- Rivalry ----------------

@event soc_rival_taunt
title: A Public Taunt
class: routine
tone: tense
cast:
  npc: any where (bond(npc) == "rival" or bond(npc) == "nemesis" or rel(npc) <= -12) and not tagged(npc, faculty)
per: npc
trigger: social
repeat: 4
art: mask
tags: rival
scene: A smirking student surrounded by a small audience, pointing at someone across a crowded dining hall.
text: In the middle of dinner, {npc} loudly recounts your most embarrassing moment of the term. People laugh. {They} look{s} very pleased.
> left: Ignore {them}
  mood -small
  say: The laughter dies down. You eat your soup with as much dignity as soup allows.
> right: Fire back
  challenge negotiate trivial:
    win:
      renown +small
      rel npc -small
      say: Your comeback is so good that someone at the far table applauds. {npc} goes scarlet.
    lose:
      renown -small
      rel npc -tiny
      say: Your comeback comes out as a squeak. The laughter doubles.

@event soc_make_peace
title: Burying the Hatchet
class: milestone
tone: tense
cast:
  npc: any where (bond(npc) == "rival" or bond(npc) == "nemesis") and rel(npc) >= 3
per: npc
trigger: social
weight: 18
art: hand
tags: rival social
scene: Two former rivals shaking hands on a dueling green at sunset, wands tucked away.
text: {npc} finds you after class, scuffing {their} shoes. "This whole rivalry thing. It's getting tiring. Truce?"
> left: Keep the edge
  rel npc -small
  say: "Thought so," {npc} says, half-smiling. The game goes on.
> right: Shake on it
  bond npc friend
  rel npc +large
  mood +small
  say: You shake. It's strange — you know {them} better than most of your friends. Maybe that's the point.

@event soc_rival_bet
title: The Wager
class: routine
tone: tense
cast:
  npc: any where bond(npc) == "rival" and not tagged(npc, faculty)
per: npc
trigger: social
repeat: 6
art: dice
tags: rival
scene: Two students slapping coins onto a table between them, a crowd gathering, a chalked tally on the wall.
text: "Ten crowns says I outscore you in the next Arcana practical," {npc} says, slapping coins on the table. A crowd forms.
> left: Decline the bet
  rel npc -tiny
  say: "Thought so." {npc} pockets the coins. You decide not to care. You care.
> right: Take the bet
  challenge spell easy:
    win:
      gold +small
      renown +small
      rel npc +small
      say: You win by a hair. {npc} pays up with a theatrical bow. "Next time."
    lose:
      gold -small
      rel npc +tiny
      say: You lose by a hair. "Next time," you say. {npc} grins. "Next time."
